index 077c6a5f05dee1e111bfacbfb4e521c7cb7670b8..f0187cfec1e41405be4bf66b9b3d939c4fe46858 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -9,6 +9,8 @@ Changelog tracking starts with 0.2.0. Prior versions were not tracked.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+- **[codex / research observation] Adds opt-in, private provider-attempt evidence for S-006 natural-outcome research.** MLX and each Ollama dispatch retain linked outcomes, pre-cleanup hashes and bounded marker-bearing artifacts, including upstream failures and rejected output. Dialogue records keep their existing response semantics with explicit stage labels and attempt joins. Startup-verified release identity stays separate from unknown activation; storage failures never change generation decisions. Source preparation only; no live activation. See `docs/provider-attempt-observation.md`.
+
 - **[codex / live verification] Repairs false USB hot-plug transitions found while aligning the pushed stack.** Minime's watcher had converted `system_profiler` timeouts into empty inventories, repeatedly inventing LifeCam removal/addition events and restarting both sensory clients. Minime commit `defd7c66` now retains the last successful per-category inventory across failed probes. Nine regressions pass; watchdog PID `41792` -> `98932` crossed three real post-activation timeouts without moving camera PID `98903` or microphone PID `98910`. After an initial host-fallback interval, those same clients naturally recovered physical capture with no unplug, daemon reset, or additional signal. Full evidence and authority limits: `docs/steward-notes/2026-09-08-usb-watchdog-timeout-live-repair.md`. No reservoir, controller, cadence, fallback-policy, prompt, model, or language-process change.
 
 - **[codex / deployment] Deploys shared SELF_STUDY parity to Astrid and Minime.** The staged release binds both adapters to one reader executable; graceful transitions replaced bridge PID 5971 with 90102 and Minime agent PID 10263 with 91125. Startup source hashes, checkpoint/session continuity and protected-service checks passed. Details and receipt hashes: `docs/steward-notes/2026-09-08-self-study-parity-live-rollout.md`. No forced study, inferred comprehension, or reservoir/controller setting change.
